    "created_at": "2016-03-14T12:25:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-14T12:25:19Z",
    "body": "FYI, `permessage-deflate; client_max_window_bits` announces the highest capability to the server. The parameter Gecko is sending represents that the server may not send the `client_max_window_bits` parameter to the client. I'm not sure what the reason it's sending the limited one now is, but it's up to implementors.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
